Historically, Hausdorff demonstrated the existence of partitions of $\mathbb{R}$ into Borel sets labeled by distinct well-ordered ordinal numbers, an insight dependent on the Well-Ordering Theorem (equivalent to the Axiom of Choice). In contrast, this paper presents solely using ZF set theory (without invoking the Axiom of Choice):
1. An application of the Well-Ordering Theorem that achieves the same result regarding these partitionings;
2. A novel method of constructing a well-ordered Borel subset of $\mathbb{R}$ with arbitrary ordinal height $\alpha$, where $\alpha < \omega_2$.
